  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently (VRCSDK-UDON-2020.06.04.14.15_Closed_Community_Test),\ndragging connecting port of a node is released on where valid port doesn't exist, it does nothing. (In other words, it cancels the edge creation).\nI suggest it opens focused-search in such case, of course with appropriate focus. And it will be useful if it connect nodes automatically after search result is selected and it creates new node.\n---- Detail\nUse case:\n1. Assuming there is a node with a output port typed `string`.\n2. You drag this port and release it on free area. \n3. Graph Editor opens search window with focusing `System.String`.\n4. You choose one of method from the searched list. For example `Contains`\n5. Graph Editor create `Contains` node, and connects the port to instance input port of `Contains` node.\nI think this behaves like auto completion in text-based programming.\n1. Input variable-name and separator (dot if in C#)\n2. Do auto-complete operation, select a method\n3. The programming tool inserts method name\nIf the port is control flow, node's type can be used as the type for focusing.\nHowever, there will be some \"irregular\" situations. for example:\n* In the case of the node denotes an Event, then focusing to Event is useless.\n* When the port is input port, then current focusing is not suitable. Maybe best way is filtering method with output type. This type of filtering is not implemented.\n* When the port is output port and typed bool, it will useful if \"Branch\" is on the list.\nSo in some cases, not focused search might be better. (Or modifier key to select search style?)",
